            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"A dedicated follower, learner, or apprentice of Jesus Christ who submits to His teachings, imitates His life, and is committed to lifelong spiritual growth and obedience.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Matthew 28:19-20\",\"Luke 14:26-27\",\"John 8:31-32\",\"John 13:35\",\"Matthew 11:29\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"A specific reference to the Twelve Apostles, serving as the foundational leaders of the Church and representing the reconstitution of the twelve tribes of Israel.\",\"basis\":[\"Matthew 10:1\",\"Luke 6:13\",\"Matthew 19:28\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"A secondary, higher tier of Christian commitment, distinguishing an entirely surrendered lordship follower from a nominal or basic believer.\",\"basis\":[\"Luke 14:25-33\",\"Matthew 16:24\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"While disciple is overwhelmingly used to describe any genuine follower of Christ (essentially synonymous with Christian in Acts), narrower usages sometimes distinguish the original Twelve or emphasize a higher standard of radical commitment in modern discipleship literature.\"}",
